# Citation metadata for the CODE in this repository.
#
# The data products are a SEPARATE Zenodo record with its own DOI and its own
# licence -- see DATA_README.md. One record carries one licence, and the data
# licence cannot be GPL (DATA_README.md, "Licence").
#
# THIS FILE IS IGNORED BY ZENODO WHENEVER .zenodo.json IS PRESENT. Zenodo does
# not merge the two: if .zenodo.json exists it builds the record from that file
# alone and never reads this one. This file drives GitHub's "Cite this
# repository" button and nothing else, so the two must be kept in step by hand.
#
# BEFORE TAGGING A RELEASE, replace every TODO- token here AND in .zenodo.json:
#   grep -rn 'TODO-' CITATION.cff .zenodo.json DATA_README.md README.md Data/README.md Results/README.md
# The GitHub-Zenodo integration publishes on release, and a published Zenodo
# record cannot be deleted -- only a new version can be added on top of it.
#
# Outstanding, and NOT guessable from anything in this repository:
#   TODO-AUTHOR-*        author list, in manuscript order
#   TODO-ORCID-*         ORCIDs (schema requires the full https://orcid.org/ URL)
#   TODO-AFFILIATION-*   affiliations
#   TODO-VERSION         git tag; no tags exist yet (`git tag -l` is empty)
#   TODO-RELEASE-DATE    date-released, added at tag time
#   (the concept DOI is now known: 10.5281/zenodo.21745158, set under `identifiers` below)
# README.md's citation block names six authors for the manuscript. It is a
# starting point, not authority: the deposit must match the accepted paper.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: >-
  Downscaled GRACE terrestrial water storage anomalies for the Ganga (Ganges) River Basin at 0.1°: Monthly and daily fields with per-pixel uncertainty, 2000–2025
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Kaushik
    given-names: P. R.
    affiliation: "CSIRO Environment, Dutton Park, Queensland 4102, Australia"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3826-7862"
  - family-names: Majumdar
    given-names: S.
    affiliation: "Division of Hydrologic Sciences, Desert Research Institute, Reno, Nevada, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3539-0147"
  - family-names: Lenczuk
    given-names: A.
    affiliation: "Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geodesy, Military University of Technology, Warsaw, Poland"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9573-1302"
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Y. K.
    affiliation: "Department of Civil Engineering, College of Engineering, Kyung Hee University, Yongin, Republic of Korea"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0038-5125"
  - family-names: Banerjee
    given-names: S.
    affiliation: "Department of Soil and Water Systems, University of Idaho-Boise, Boise, Idaho, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6139-8403"
  - family-names: Thakur
    given-names: P. K.
    affiliation: "Water Resources Department, Indian Institute of Remote Sensing, ISRO, Dehradun, India"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2719-7021"
  # Names and order follow the manuscript citation. Every ORCID was checked
  # against its ISO 7064 MOD 11-2 check digit before being written here.

abstract: >-
  Code for a 0.1 degree monthly and daily terrestrial water storage anomaly
  (TWSA) product over the Ganga (Ganges) river basin, 2000-2025. GRACE and
  GRACE-FO JPL RL06 mascons are spatially downscaled by fitting a
  predictor-TWSA relation across mascons with tree ensembles, and every
  mascon's area-weighted aggregate is then forced back onto the observed
  value. The monthly field is disaggregated to daily under an exact monthly
  constraint, its within-month shape supplied by the ERA5-Land water balance
  with nothing fitted. Per-pixel uncertainty is reported as separate terms
  rather than one number, because only some of them are measurable against an
  observation. Fine spatial structure is inferred from ERA5-Land and GLDAS,
  not observed, and agreement with GRACE at mascon scale is imposed by mass
  conservation rather than earned; the held-out evidence is a
  leave-one-mascon-out cross-validation over 19 mascons and a comparison
  against 656 quality-controlled CGWB dug wells.

version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-01
#   Left absent rather than stubbed: the schema requires a real date here, so a
#   placeholder string would fail validation outright.
license: CC-BY-4.0
# The record bundles code and data. CC-BY-4.0 describes the DATA; the source
# code in the same archive stays GPL-3.0-only under its own LICENSE file.
# A Zenodo record has one licence field, so the carve-out lives in the
# description rather than here.
# GPL-3.0-only, not -or-later: LICENSE is the verbatim GPLv3 text and no "or
# later" notice appears in any source file or in LICENSE's own application
# section. If the notice is wanted, add it BEFORE the release -- the archive is
# permanent. See TODO.md D2.

repository-code: "https://github.com/montimaj/grace-grb"
url: "https://github.com/montimaj/grace-grb"

# The VERSION DOI is what a paper should cite: it pins v1.0.0 rather than
# whatever was released last. The concept DOI is the "all versions" line and is
# listed second.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21745159

identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21745159
    description: Version DOI for v1.0.0 - cite this one
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21745158
    description: Concept DOI, resolving to the latest version of this record

keywords:
  - GRACE
  - GRACE-FO
  - terrestrial water storage
  - groundwater depletion
  - spatial downscaling
  - temporal disaggregation
  - Ganga basin
  - Ganges river basin
  - machine learning
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - ERA5-Land
  - uncertainty quantification
